 lot of  terrorism  and president trump's gone very very  tough at it because his priority  is protecting american citizens so  president trump the deal maker  had a very big victory yesterday and was  able to bring our close ally  uh united arab emirates together with  our closest ally in the region israel  which will make america safer in the  region  and the whole region more hopeful  president netanyahu  says israel is still committed to  annexing parts of the west bank but  it can only happen in coordination with  the u.s and some are saying  since he's still committed to that this  is really only a symbolic victory  well not at all first of all you have  the first peace agreement in 26 years so  that's not symbolic that's concrete  but with regards to the annexation the  middle east has a lot of problems these  are problems that have been developed  over  decades and president trump's the first  person to come in very pragmatic he  moved the embassy to jerusalem he  recognized the golan heights  he ended the disastrous iran deal which  gave 150 billion dollars  to the largest state sponsor of  terrorism that chance death to america  death to israel and so president trump's  really realigned things he's also  combated  extremism he's taken out some of the  leading terrorists in the region  and that's created a much better  paradigm there so we still have to deal  with the realities on the ground we  still have a lot more work to do but  over the last three and a half years  president trump's strategy that he laid  out  in riyadh in 2017 has really been  working  and we have a lot more successes ahead  and that's why president trump's  strategy which a lot of people  discounted and under  estimated because it was unorthodox is  something that is proving to have great  results as tom friedman  called out in his column today i want to  turn to the coronavirus  because we just had the worst day for  deaths since late may  the cdc head uh robert redfield said we  could face the worst  fall in his in the history of american  health if we don't follow some basic  guidelines  and dr anthony fauci said i'm not  pleased with things are  how things are going vice president  biden in his campaign has called for a  national mass  mandate the president said he is against  that  why president trump has strongly  encouraged people to wear masks  he believes in the federalist system he  trusts americans to make the right  decisions for themselves  he trusts governors to make the right  decisions a lot of governors have put in  place mass mandates  and the president has supported them but  you have some states that have very low  transmission you have some states that  are very high and if people feel more  comfortable wearing masks  they absolutely should i do think it's a  public health  a good thing to do people should be  doing it  but president trump does not believe  that washington should be telling people  how to live their lives in all the  different states so  i i think that this is people really  politicizing this issue more than  anything else  i think we have made a lot of progress  we've gotten uh you know to the  hospitals to our country  all the different uh supplies that they  needed we've seen a lot of hysteria that  that wouldn't be possible president  trump's led  the effort to do a vaccine the fastest  vaccine in history took 13 months  to get from development to stage 3  trials on the coronavirus vaccine  president trump's done that in four  months without  bypassing any safety regulations and we  have six of them now  that are very close to being done and  we're simultaneously manufacturing doses  so that the minute it gets approved  uh we'll be able to start making it  available to those who want it so  look president trump is is making his  decisions based on the science he's been  following the advice of his advisors  he's focused on making sure that people  as few people as possible  lose their jobs and that the 